  "validationNotes": [
    "First Windows full run: 2342 tests, 2282 passed, 59 failed, one skipped. Old rule expectations were updated; a real incompatibility in the clan-chest validator required version 5 while preserving versions 2–4. Two unrelated Windows atomic-rename EPERM failures are retained; final Linux full run is green.",
    "Targeted Windows rerun initially had two outdated expected greatness/accessory values; the two affected files then passed 9/9.",
    "Browser checks initially caught an extra CSS scale on VIP icons and a fixture using the default avatar. Both fixed. Mismatched bundled Playwright and installed browsers caused separate tooling failures; matching cached Playwright 1.65.1 passed all three engines.",
    "The only source change after the full Linux run was CRLF/LF normalization in one CSS file, with no declaration changes.",
    "An initial service query used the nonexistent heroether-game name; the actual heroether-play service was healthy. No recovery action was taken for that mistaken query.",
    "Prior backups, development comments and historical chest promises were retained. New expressive emote animations are previews only.",
    "The first 40-second startup wait expired; subsequent readiness checks succeeded without a restart. The retained old localhost review process had no listener on 3104; its isolated data was backed up and it was replaced with the reviewed source. The unrelated experimental process was not touched.",
    "Post-install samples have zero connected players and verify service health only, not load capacity."
